RULE APlayerIdentifierIsTheSteamAccountOrTheNetworkClient
	HOLDS_FOR all
	DOMAIN game
	DOMAIN format
	SPEC "a player identifier is the Steam account identifier of the player when the game runs"
		+ "under Steam, and the network client identifier of the player otherwise"
		ATTESTED_BY "packages/core-mapping/src/save/infrastructure/wireFormat/schemas/section2-players.schema.json::the"
			+ "Steam ID under Steam, the network client id otherwise"
	APPLIES_TO_SECTION @SECTION.Players
	RATIONALE "An account carries the same identifier in every save it plays, and without Steam the"
		+ "host is client 0 of every game and a client id is given again in a later session, so an"
		+ "identifier is unique neither across two saves nor, formally, within one; a save written"
		+ "before multiplayer carries no identifier, which the game reads as 0"
	SOURCE "Game assembly Assembly-CSharp.dll of release 2.103, Steam build 25296421, decompiled on"
		+ "2026-10-04: PlayerMainController.OnNetworkSpawn sets the identifier to"
		+ "SteamUser.GetSteamID() when SteamManager.Initialized, otherwise to"
		+ "NetworkObject.OwnerClientId; JSONExport inserts an id of 0 into the player entry of a"
		+ "save written before multiplayer"
		REF @GAME_RELEASE.2.103
	SOURCE "Extracted from the ruling on player identity, decision of 2026-09-07"
		PR 39
